derivations.claim:
Because $F$ and $G$ are compact, hence bounded, $A=G\circ F$ is compact: the image under $F$ of any bounded sequence is bounded, and compactness of $G$ gives a subsequence whose images under $G$ converge. Put $a_j=\lambda_j\mu_j$ and $w_j=\langle w,x_jangle$. The adjoint identity [F6] and the singular-vector equations show $N(F)=\{x_j:j\in J\}^{\perp}$ and $N(G)=\{y_j:j\in J\}^{\perp}$: each kernel vector is orthogonal to the indicated family, and conversely a vector orthogonal to the family is orthogonal to the full range of the adjoint, hence is killed by the operator. Since $G$ is injective on $\overline{R(F)}=\overline{R(G^*)}$ (its coefficients there are the positive $\mu_j$), $\ker A=\ker F$; hence $(x_j)$ is a basis of $N(A)^\perp$. By [F1], $Ax_j=a_jz_j$. The adjoint identity [F6] gives $A^*=F^*G^*$, so [F5] yields $A^*z_j=a_jx_j$, $A^*Ax_j=a_j^2x_j$, and $|A|x_j=a_jx_j$. The vectors $z_j$ span $\overline{R(A)}$, since the range of $A$ is generated by $Ax_j=a_jz_j$ and $a_j>0$. Compact spectral calculus and [F3] therefore give $x^\dagger=\sum_{j\in J}a_j^
u w_jx_j$ and $z=Ax^\dagger=\sum_{j\in J}a_j^{
u+1}w_jz_j$. The source element is perpendicular to $\ker A$, so [F4] gives $A^\dagger z=x^\dagger$. Thus $y^\dagger=Fx^\dagger$ lies in $N(G)^\perp$ and $x^\dagger$ lies in $N(F)^\perp$; since $Gy^\dagger=z$ and $Fx^\dagger=y^\dagger$, the minimum-norm property [F4] gives $G^\dagger z=y^\dagger$ and $F^\dagger y^\dagger=x^\dagger$. Finally, $v:=\sum_j\lambda_j^{
u+1}w_jy_j$ satisfies $y^\dagger=|G|^
u v$ and $\|v\|^2=\sum_j\lambda_j^{2
u+2}|w_j|^2\le\|w\|^2\leho^2$.
